<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net48;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>12</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>Aspose.Pdf</RootNamespace>

    <!-- Package / release metadata -->
    <PackageId>Aspose.PDF.FOSS</PackageId>
    <Version>26.11.0</Version>
    <Product>Aspose.PDF FOSS for .NET</Product>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
26.11.0 - fidelity release: XFA forms, HTML in and out, PDF/A and text.

New: LinkAnnotation.Hyperlink; UpdateAppearances on underline and squiggly annotations; ChoiceField.SetValue; StructureElement.Remove; Page.ProcessSpecialSymbols; ExtGState.FillOpacity and StrokeOpacity; PdfFunction.ClampInput and ClampOutput; ImageLoadException, raised for image bytes no decoder can read instead of an image that silently draws nothing.
XFA: dynamic forms render and convert to standard forms closer to their design - load-time scripts run before the pages are painted, fields and text draws continue across content areas and pages, captions, check boxes and radio buttons take the sizes they declare, and a converted form lists exactly the fields its template defines, filled from their data bindings.
HTML: HTML-to-PDF and HTML import read more real-world pages - stylesheet selectors and exclusions, list markers, preformatted blocks that clip, form controls at their CSS sizes, bordered, spanning and block-laid table cells; PDF-to-HTML ships the fonts widget appearances use, keeps right-to-left text in its order and keeps page text out of PNG backgrounds; SVG import handles nested svg viewports, symbols drawn through use, text-only foreignObject and SVG images in data URIs.
PDF/A and fonts: conversions repair TrueType and Type 1 font dictionaries (CharSet, CIDToGIDMap, encodings), restate soft masks and trim oversized Indexed palettes; the standard Asian faces are found by name; font fallback prefers installed broad-coverage faces and never puts a fixed-pitch face in place of a proportional one.
Text: replacements keep right-to-left lines shaped and in visual order and move the rest of their line by the width they gained; sub- and superscripts set on a segment draw as scripts; auto-tagging reads raised marks, list labels and suffixes on the lines they belong to; the table absorber finds column boundaries and spanned cells inside ruled tables.
Signing and redaction: SHA-1 PKCS#1 and PKCS#7 signatures are written as their handlers define, a nested signature field is found by its full name, and a signing update keeps the form dictionary's entries; an applied redaction draws its overlay appearance and removes its own mark, and JPEG images in CMYK, palette or Lab colour stay lossless in their own colour space.
Also: CMYK colours are written as CMYK; generated layouts read correctly on rotated pages; rendering fixes for clip paths, thin strokes and indexed images; faster saves of dense pages, duplicate-stream optimization and XFA field reads.

Full release notes: https://github.com/aspose-pdf-foss/Aspose.PDF-FOSS-for-.NET/releases/tag/v26.11.0
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Aspose</Authors>
    <Company>Aspose Pty Ltd</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Aspose Pty Ltd</Copyright>
    <Description>A free, open-source PDF library for .NET Framework 4.8, .NET Standard 2.0 and .NET 8+: read, create, modify, and render PDF documents. Some features are incomplete and the public API may change between releases.</Description>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/aspose-pdf-foss/Aspose.PDF-FOSS-for-.NET</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/aspose-pdf-foss/Aspose.PDF-FOSS-for-.NET.git</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>pdf;aspose;pdf-library;acroform;pdf-a;document;foss</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Packed into the NuGet package when/if `dotnet pack` is run; inert for plain builds. -->
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

<ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Aspose.Pdf.Foss.Tests" Condition="'$(ExcludeInternalsVisibleTo)' != 'true'" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Without InternalsVisibleTo the compiler warns (CS0649) on internal fields a friend
       assembly could assign; suppress it in the pack build so the DLL stays identical. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(ExcludeInternalsVisibleTo)' == 'true'">
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS0649</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

<!-- Runtime dependencies. System.Drawing.Common is the only one on the modern targets;
     netstandard2.0 and net48 add the packages that carry APIs their BCL lacks
     (System.Text.Json, Span, PKCS#7, code-page encodings, HashCode). -->
<ItemGroup>
  <PackageReference Include="System.Drawing.Common" Version="8.0.0" />
</ItemGroup>
<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' Or '$(TargetFramework)' == 'net48'">
  <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="8.0.5" />
  <PackageReference Include="System.Memory" Version="4.5.5" />
  <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="8.0.2" />
  <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Encoding.CodePages" Version="8.0.0" />
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Bcl.HashCode" Version="6.0.0" />
  <!-- Build-time only (PrivateAssets=all): they add nothing to the shipped package.
       The first generates the C# language-feature types the old BCLs lack (IsExternalInit,
       Index/Range, RequiredMember, the OS-platform attributes); the second supplies the
       newer BCL convenience overloads as source (string.Contains(char), Stream.Write(Span),
       KeyValuePair.Deconstruct, ...). Everything they cannot cover lives in src/Compat. -->
  <PackageReference Include="PolySharp" Version="1.16.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
  <PackageReference Include="Polyfill" Version="7.33.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
</ItemGroup>
<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net48'">
  <Reference Include="System.Net.Http" />
</ItemGroup>
<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' Or '$(TargetFramework)' == 'net48'">
  <PolySharpIncludeRuntimeSupportedAttributes>true</PolySharpIncludeRuntimeSupportedAttributes>
  <!-- The polyfill sources use C# 13 features; the language level of the modern targets is unchanged. -->
  <LangVersion>13</LangVersion>
  <!-- CS0436: RuntimeHelpers.GetSubArray (the array range operator) is declared in src/Compat for these
       targets and shadows the BCL type that lacks it. -->
  <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS0436</NoWarn>
  <!-- The old reference assemblies carry no nullability annotations (no [NotNullWhen] on
       string.IsNullOrEmpty, TryGetValue, ...), so flow analysis there reports what the
       annotated modern targets prove safe. The modern targets keep full checking of the
       same source. -->
  <Nullable>annotations</Nullable>
</PropertyGroup>

<!-- SonarSource's C# rules - the same engine a SonarQube server applies, delivered as
     analyzers that run inside the compiler. OFF unless asked for: a first analysis of a
     library this size reports thousands of findings, and TreatWarningsAsErrors above
     would turn every one of them into a build error. Every ordinary build - the test
     jobs, pack, sign, the compat harness - therefore sees the project exactly as before.

     To read the findings:
       dotnet build src/Aspose.Pdf.Foss.csproj -c Release -p:RunSonarAnalyzer=true \
         -p:TreatWarningsAsErrors=false "-p:ErrorLog=issues.sarif%2Cversion=2.1"
     or run the sonar-issues job, which renders that SARIF into a report by rule.

     The findings are advisory. Promoting a chosen subset to real warnings belongs in
     .editorconfig, deliberately, once the backlog has been read. -->
<ItemGroup Condition="'$(RunSonarAnalyzer)' == 'true'">
  <PackageReference Include="SonarAnalyzer.CSharp" Version="10.33.0.1635" PrivateAssets="all" />
</ItemGroup>

<ItemGroup>
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Devices\CmykToRgbLut.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Operators\CmykOperatorColors.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\DjVuDingbats.ttf" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.DjVuDingbats.ttf" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\AdobeCid.Japan1.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.AdobeCid.Japan1.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\AdobeCid.CNS1.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.AdobeCid.CNS1.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\AdobeCid.GB1.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.AdobeCid.GB1.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\AdobeCid.Korea1.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.AdobeCid.Korea1.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\AdobeGlyphList.txt" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.AdobeGlyphList.txt" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\CMap.UniJIS-UCS2-H.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.CMap.UniJIS-UCS2-H.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\CMap.90ms-RKSJ-H.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.CMap.90ms-RKSJ-H.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\CMap.UniGB-UCS2-H.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.CMap.UniGB-UCS2-H.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\CMap.GBK-EUC-H.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.CMap.GBK-EUC-H.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\CMap.UniCNS-UCS2-H.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.CMap.UniCNS-UCS2-H.bin" />
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Text\Resources\CMap.UniKS-UCS2-H.bin" LogicalName="Aspose.Pdf.Text.Resources.CMap.UniKS-UCS2-H.bin" />
</ItemGroup>

  <!-- Force a full rebuild of this project on EVERY build, even when no source
       has changed. Two layers can otherwise skip the build:
         1) DisableFastUpToDateCheck stops Visual Studio short-circuiting via its
            fast up-to-date check, so VS always invokes MSBuild on this project.
         2) Deleting the intermediate assembly before CoreCompile defeats
            MSBuild's own incremental compile, forcing the C# compiler to run.
       Trade-off: every build recompiles this project, so builds/test runs are
       slower. Remove this block to return to normal incremental builds. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <DisableFastUpToDateCheck>true</DisableFastUpToDateCheck>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="ForceAlwaysRecompile" BeforeTargets="CoreCompile">
    <Delete Files="@(IntermediateAssembly)" />
  </Target>

</Project>
